query:
UPDATE services SET
  faqs = '[{"q":"How often should catch basins be cleaned?","a":"For most residential properties, once a year is sufficient. Commercial properties with high traffic or large impervious surfaces may need cleaning twice a year. Municipal catch basins on heavily used roads are typically cleaned annually as part of a scheduled maintenance program. If you are seeing slow drainage or standing water after rain, the basin likely needs attention sooner."},{"q":"What happens if a catch basin is not cleaned regularly?","a":"Sediment and debris accumulate in the basin sump over time. Once the sump fills, debris starts to block the outlet pipe and the grate opening. The result is surface flooding during rain events, which can damage pavement, erode landscaping, and allow water to enter buildings. In winter, blocked basins contribute to ice formation on driveways and parking lots."},{"q":"Can you clean a catch basin that has been neglected for years?","a":"Yes. Heavily silted basins take longer to clean and may require multiple passes with the vac truck, but we handle them regularly. In some cases where sediment has hardened, we use high-pressure flushing to break it up before vacuuming. We will assess the condition on arrival and give you an honest estimate of the work required."},{"q":"Do you repair catch basins as well as clean them?","a":"Yes. We repair cracked basin walls, replace deteriorated frames and grates, and reline basins that have structural damage. Where repairs are straightforward, we carry them out on the same visit as the cleaning. For more extensive reconstruction, we schedule a follow-up appointment."},{"q":"What is the difference between a catch basin and a storm sewer?","a":"A catch basin is the surface collection point, typically the grated inlet you see in a parking lot or at the curb. The storm sewer is the underground pipe network that the catch basin drains into. Catch basin cleaning addresses the collection point and the short outlet pipe. Storm sewer cleaning and inspection is a separate service that we also provide."},{"q":"How long does catch basin cleaning take?","a":"A single residential catch basin typically takes 30 to 60 minutes to clean. Commercial properties with multiple basins take longer depending on the number of basins and their condition. We give you a time estimate when we schedule the job."},{"q":"Is catch basin cleaning covered by insurance or required by the municipality?","a":"In most cases, catch basin maintenance on private property is the responsibility of the property owner and is not covered by standard property insurance. Some municipalities require property owners to maintain catch basins on their property in working order and may issue notices of violation if a basin is blocked and causing drainage problems onto public property."},{"q":"Do you provide catch basin cleaning for condominium corporations and property management companies?","a":"Yes. We work with property management companies, condominium corporations, and commercial landlords across Southwestern Ontario. We can set up annual service agreements that cover all catch basins on a property and provide documentation for your maintenance records."},{"q":"What do you do with the material removed from the catch basin?","a":"The sediment and debris we remove is transported in our vac truck and disposed of at an approved facility. We handle all waste disposal as part of the service."},{"q":"What areas do you serve for catch basin cleaning?","a":"We serve residential, commercial, and municipal clients across London and Southwestern Ontario, including the City of London, Strathroy, St. Thomas, Woodstock, and surrounding communities. Contact us to confirm service availability in your area."}]'
WHERE slug = 'catch-basin-cleaning';

